      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_Hill%2C_Texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Forest Hill incorporated as a village on March 16, 1946, and grew to a city by 1949 after reaching 500 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_Hill%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 1949 petition led to the village’s relabeling as a city on April 8, marking a new chapter in local governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_Hill%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A bond election authorized the city to buy the private water system from the Texas Water Company, securing reliable water for residents.",
